    "turn_text": "surprised me. Yeah, you're right. And it tends to be like from the anti-GMO crowd or the anti-vax crowd. And that is one of these things where the far right circumnavigates the globe and comes around to the far left sometimes on vaccines. But it's fringe stuff. And even in my district, which 20 years ago, 10 years ago, that was maybe the heart of the anti-vaxx movement. It's not now. Marin County, my home county, actually led the nation in vaccination during the COVID crisis when the vaccine came out. So we have evolved and we have very much embraced science and public health and common sense when it comes to these things. The tooth decay thing, though, My first position as an elected official was on my local water board. And I made the mistake as a board member, the Marine Municipal Water District, of allowing a so-called scientist on the fluoride issue to come to one of our board meetings and present on fluoride. And I think the fire marshal had to be called because the room was so packed with people. And it was a fight, basically, a food fight between folks who thought that fluoride was killing people and was this terrible chemical additive that is, you know, Dr. Strange Love is putting into the water supply. and dentists and pediatricians and others who brought real science to the conversation and explained what happens when you don't Florida water and what happens especially to poor kids in underserved neighborhoods and what that means to their health outcomes and to their success in life if you follow the data. So we continue to fluoridate water in the part of Marin that I represented on that water board. And if I can have anything to do with it, we'll continue to oppose dumb anti-science ideas to ban fluoride from water supplies.",
